         dict(ans="(a) **Sweep then bearish displacement.** Candle A penetrated PDH by a wick (2,398.9) and closed back below it at 2,394.2 — a valid sweep. Candles B and C are consecutive bearish closes with wide bodies: confirmation. (b) Invalidation above the **sweep high of 2,398.9** (with a buffer in practice), because that is the price that, if closed above, would mean the market accepted the higher area. (c) If candle A had closed *above* 2,396.4 — say at 2,397.1 — and candle B had held above it, this would have been a **run**, and the short would have been the wrong trade."),
